📰 Fake News Detection using NLP & Machine Learning:

An NLP-based machine learning project that classifies news articles as Fake or Real using text preprocessing, TF-IDF feature extraction, and multiple machine learning/deep learning models.

📌 Project Overview:

The project uses a dataset containing 44,898 news articles, including 23,481 fake and 21,417 real articles.

The text data is processed and transformed into numerical representations before being used to train and compare different classification models.

🧠 Models Implemented
SVM with TF-IDF
ANN with TF-IDF
ANN with Trainable Embeddings
Bidirectional LSTM (BiLSTM)
1D CNN with Embeddings
Transformer Encoder
🔧 Technologies Used
Python
